config FREETZ_PACKAGE_OT_BR_POSIX
	bool "OpenThread Border Router (ot-br-posix) 2026.10.0"
	depends on FREETZ_TARGET_UCLIBC_1_0_58_MIN
	select FREETZ_PACKAGE_OPENTHREAD
	select FREETZ_LIB_STDCXXLIB
	select FREETZ_LIB_libatomic
	select FREETZ_LIB_libpthread  if FREETZ_TARGET_UCLIBC_HAS_multiple_libs
	select FREETZ_LIB_libutil     if FREETZ_TARGET_UCLIBC_HAS_multiple_libs
	select FREETZ_LIB_librt       if FREETZ_TARGET_UCLIBC_HAS_multiple_libs
	default n
	help
		ot-br-posix is the OpenThread Border Router for Linux: otbr-agent
		attaches an 802.15.4 Radio Co-Processor (RCP) and connects the
		Thread mesh network to the IPv6 home network, so that Thread
		devices can be reached from the LAN.

		Installed binaries:

		 - /usr/sbin/otbr-agent   the Border Router daemon
		 - /usr/sbin/ot-ctl       control client (talks to otbr-agent)

		The Freetz configuration page offers the settings needed to start
		the agent: the infrastructure interface (default br0), the spinel
		URL of the RCP (default spinel+hdlc+uart:///dev/ttyACM0), the boot
		wait time for the RCP device and extra command line options.

		Runtime requirements on the Fritz!Box:

		 - an 802.15.4 RCP (for example an nRF52840 dongle) flashed with
		   the OpenThread RCP firmware, connected over USB/serial
		 - /dev/net/tun (the agent creates the Thread interface wpan0)
		 - IPv6 forwarding (net.ipv6.conf.all.forwarding=1)

		This is the Thread side of a Matter installation: Matter/Thread
		devices become reachable for a Matter controller (for example
		python-matter-server, which the Domoticz Matter driver talks to).

		All optional upstream components (D-Bus API, web GUI, REST server,
		NAT64, DHCPv6-PD, backbone router, nftables firewall) are disabled,
		which avoids the protobuf, dbus, jsoncpp, cJSON, cpp-httplib and
		libsystemd dependencies entirely. mDNS/DNS-SD is served by the
		OpenThread core (OTBR_MDNS=openthread), so no Avahi or
		mDNSResponder port is required.

		Can be externalized (External menu): otbr-agent (2.4 MB) and ot-ctl are
		moved to external storage; the agent takes its radio URL and
		infrastructure interface from the Freetz configuration.
